 milestone_doc: |
-  Operator directive 2026-06-12: graft the resumable-training fix into the next milestone. .380
-  PROVED the nano-trm trainer mechanism works (exp4107: real checkpoint, exact_accuracy 1.0 on the
-  4x4 smoke, 742s) BUT the published Sudoku-Extreme baseline did NOT reproduce: exp4108 trained ~57
-  min, hit the conductor's ~80-min wall-clock cap (interrupted_return_code_1), and reached only
-  0.0232 exact-accuracy vs the 0.87 target. The blocker is INFRASTRUCTURE, not nano-trm: the
-  reproduction needs more CONTIGUOUS training than a single conductor task allows.
+  Operator directive 2026-06-12: graft a resume-correctness diagnostic into the next milestone
+  before committing to more training passes. .381 proved the resumable MECHANISM runs (passes
+  resume from the stable checkpoint, epoch counter continues) BUT val only crawled 2.3% -> 9.7% ->
+  10.6% over three bounded passes, far below the published 0.87.
 
-  THE FIX (this milestone): RESUMABLE multi-task training. nano-trm's train.py accepts
-  `ckpt_path=` (verified: `trainer.fit(..., ckpt_path=cfg.get("ckpt_path"))`). Each resume task:
-  (1) writes the checkpoint to a STABLE shared path `results/trm_runs/sudoku_extreme_baseline/`
-  (NOT a per-run hydra dir -- that is why .380 could not resume); (2) resumes from that checkpoint
-  if it exists; (3) BOUNDS its own training to <=60 min via `trainer.max_time` (fallback:
-  max_steps tuned to ~55 min) so it stops CLEANLY and saves BEFORE the 80-min conductor cap fires;
-  (4) reports cumulative epochs + best val exact-accuracy. Three resume passes (~3h GPU total)
-  accumulate toward 0.87; the dataset (nano-trm/data/sudoku_extreme_1k_aug_1k) is already generated
-  so no regen. ACCUMULATE FLOOR: if val exact-accuracy does NOT improve across a pass, flag it
-  (config/data problem) rather than burning more GPU; if .381 ends below 0.87, .382 continues from
-  the stable checkpoint (accumulate-across-milestones).
+  ROOT CAUSE (outer-loop diagnostic, 2026-06-13, from the .381 metrics CSVs): the LR SCHEDULER
+  RE-WARMS each resume pass. train/lr resets to the IDENTICAL 2.45e-6 warmup value at the start of
+  every pass and ramps to 4.95e-6 -- identical across pass1/pass2/pass3 -- even though the epoch
+  counter continues correctly (4049->4099->4149->...). So Lightning restores the optimizer/global
+  step on `ckpt_path` resume, but the LR schedule restarts its warmup each pass instead of
+  continuing the global decay schedule. Three bounded passes are therefore NOT equivalent to one
+  contiguous run: the model keeps re-warming a tiny LR and never follows the intended schedule ->
+  glacial convergence.
 
-  THEN graft (exp4119, DEFENSIVE read): only if the accumulated baseline is faithful (val within
-  tolerance of 0.87, or >=0.85) does the Carnot Sudoku verifier graft run (rerank + A=verifier-cert
-  vs B=vote-cert de-confound, on Sudoku where the verifier is an EXACT executable check). If the
-  baseline is still accumulating, the graft is DEFERRED honestly (no hard block) and .382 picks up.
+  THE FIX (exp4126, headline): make the LR schedule CONTINUE across resumes (state-restored /
+  global-step-based), not re-warm. Inspect nano-trm's scheduler config (src/nn/configs/model/trm.yaml
+  + experiment config) + how src/nn/train.py constructs/restores the scheduler on resume; fix so a
+  resumed pass continues the schedule from where the prior pass left off; VALIDATE by reading the
+  metrics CSV of a fresh resumed pass and confirming train/lr does NOT reset to the warmup value but
+  continues monotonically. ONLY THEN (exp4127) resume accumulation toward 0.87 with the corrected
+  schedule.
 
-  ACHIEVABLE OUTCOMES (no over-promise): (a) the resumable mechanism works end-to-end (val climbs
-  across passes, checkpoint resumes cleanly); (b) the published ~0.87 baseline reproduced + persisted
-  at the stable path; (c) the verifier graft beats / ties the ablation, OR is deferred because the
-  baseline has not yet converged. Any of these is decision-grade and honest.
+  HONEST ALTERNATIVE (if bounded-resume fundamentally cannot carry this schedule): exp4126 may find
+  the right fix is NOT bounded-resume at all but a single longer CONTIGUOUS run (a monitored detached
+  training job outside the conductor's 80-min task cap, OR a shorter-horizon config that converges in
+  one pass). If so, report that honestly as the recommended path rather than forcing the re-warm fix.
+
+  ACHIEVABLE OUTCOMES (no over-promise): (a) the LR-resume fix lands and a resumed pass shows a
+  CONTINUOUS schedule (the prerequisite for effective accumulation); (b) with the fix, val climbs
+  materially faster than the .381 +1pp/pass and approaches 0.87; (c) the verifier graft runs on a
+  faithful baseline, or is honestly deferred. Any is decision-grade.
 
